    q: "Why must assets always equal liabilities plus equity?",
    a: "Because every asset is funded by someone: creditors, whose claim is a liability, or owners, whose claim is equity. Double-entry bookkeeping records every transaction in at least two accounts with equal effects, so the equation holds after each one. Equity is the residual: book assets minus every liability.",
