    a: "Basic EPS divides net income available to common shareholders by the weighted average shares outstanding. Diluted EPS also counts the shares that options, warrants, RSUs and convertibles would add if exercised or converted, but only those that would lower EPS. Diluted EPS is the more conservative figure and the usual basis for P/E.",
