    why: "The indirect method is easier to produce from accrual books and shows exactly why profit and cash differ, which analysts value. The direct method is more intuitive, and standard setters encourage it, but US GAAP requires a company that uses it to also present the reconciliation from net income, so few bother. For modeling, the indirect layout is what you build: it links naturally to the income statement and the balance sheet changes.",
